From: Daniel Campos Ramos <Capitain_Jack@yahoo.com>
Date: Wed, 25 Nov 2026 01:10:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] autotests: a networked output is a screen like the others

A network screen (an output the screencast protocol's version 7 request makes without the split-eye
flag, such as a Cast device thrown to) is checked as a monitor would be: test_virtual_output_properties
gains networkedOutput (the 3D formats and the eye swap offered, 2D at the device mode, the format twins
made from the switches and taken away again) and networkedChoiceKeptByIdentity (the format, switches and
swap chosen for a device come back at the next output for the same device, not for another device and
not at another mode); screencasting_test gains testNetworkedOutput (a declared pair, left eye red and
right eye blue, in a frame of the stream for 2D and every format, with and without the swap); the new
integration test testThrowToMenu checks the window menu's two lists.
Red on +65: the formats cannot be switched on, the store forces 2D, the menu lists the device under
Move to Screen. The headset's split-eye rows are unchanged and pass on both.

Assisted-by: Claude Opus 5.5
